.TH "SKARN-LICENSE" "1" "2026-06-23" "skarn 0.17.0" "Skarn Manual"
.SH NAME
skarn\-license \- Show the active license, or install one from a file (or
stdin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskarn\fR \fBlicense\fR [<file>|\-] [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the active license, or install one from a file (or stdin).
.PP
Show the active license, or install one. With no argument it reports what
license this machine is using, where it came from, and when it expires. With a
file argument (or \- to read stdin) it validates the license and installs it
to the config directory, backing up any license already there. It never prints
the license token itself, and it works without a license, so it never exits 5.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Replace an already\-installed license without asking. Required when installing
over an existing license from a script or from stdin, where there is no
terminal to confirm on.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the license status as a single JSON object (state, tier, licensee, org,
seats, license id, issue and expiry dates, days remaining, and the source it
was resolved from). The license token is never included.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
skarn(1)
